design\releases\0_2_0\card__1ebcfe45-9445-47e6-8619-6c72708bd91b.json:84:          "content": "design/feature_descriptions\\B_100_claude_agent_shows_all_responses_double.md:13:When an action is run by the claude agent, all responses, accept the last one he gives are shown 2 times in the chatlog. so 2 identical bubbles below each other.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_100_claude_agent_shows_all_responses_double.md:42:* Running a Claude action produces exactly one chatlog bubble per assistant step; no step (except formerly the last) is duplicated.\ndesktop\\test_agent_spawn.mjs:5:const prompt = '\"Reply with exactly: spawn \"test\" ok\"';\ndesktop\\test_agent_spawn.mjs:7:    ? ['exec', '--json', prompt]\ndesktop\\test_agent_spawn.mjs:8:    : ['--print', '--verbose', '--output-format', 'stream-json', prompt];\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:15:when you close and re-open an action popup, the selected agent configuration is lost and appears to go back to default.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:19:`ActionPopupContent` creates a new `ActionRunInputStore` for each action/context mount. Selector changes update that store, but closing the popup destroys it. Reopening creates an empty snapshot, so `useActionRunSettings` resolves agent, model, thinking level, access level, and approval policy from the action definition and desktop defaults again.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:28:* Popup roots perform only stable store lookup and never subscribe. Selector, prompt, phrase, preset-name, disabled-message, and bottom-row owners use `useSyncExternalStore` at their leaf boundary when they consume settings. Event handlers send field-change commands to central store; they never mutate snapshots or activity objects.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_101_action_agent_selectors_forget_settings.md:46:* Project, folder, and regular-file action popups keep current session-only selector behavior.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_107_steering_prompts_disappear.md:5:title: steering prompts disappear\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_107_steering_prompts_disappear.md:14:When an agent is running and we send a steering prompt to it, the prompt just disappears until the backend reports back that it has been sent. this is super annoying.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_107_steering_prompts_disappear.md:16:instead, we should put it in a wait queue, shown visually on the ui by already adding the prompt to the chatlog, but in a 'in transit' state, with a button to 'steer' which should send it immediately.  Otherwise, the prompt will be sent after the next waitforInput state\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_121_add_support_for_placeholders_in_the_action_input_box.md:15:when user enters {{, the placeholder selection box should be shown, just like in the prompt editor\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_120_add_this_card_placeholder.md:18:- Electron recognizes `{{card-file}}`, but not `{{this-card}}`. Because unknown placeholders remain literal, agent prompts and commands currently pass `{{this-card}}` through unchanged.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_120_add_this_card_placeholder.md:19:- Action prompt editors offer `{{card-file}}` through typeahead and toolbar insertion; `{{this-card}}` is absent from their shared placeholder catalog.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_120_add_this_card_placeholder.md:24:- Add `this-card` to Electron's recognized card placeholder names. Resolve both `{{this-card}}` and `{{card-file}}` from the same required `context.file` value in the shared resolver, so stored prompts, edited prompts, and commands receive identical paths.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_120_add_this_card_placeholder.md:29:- Test shared resolution, missing context, prompt and command execution paths, and editor insertion availability.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_120_add_this_card_placeholder.md:33:- Given card context with `file: 'design/card.md'`, both `{{this-card}}` and `{{card-file}}` resolve to `design/card.md` in agent prompts and action commands.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_120_add_this_card_placeholder.md:34:- Stored prompts and prompts edited in the Action popup resolve `{{this-card}}` before agent process start.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\activity\\card__56dd54b0-9554-4545-85d4-bb45efef4d6e.json:17:            \"design/feature_descriptions/B_85_add_the_reference_to_a_chatlog_to_a_card_as_soon_as_possible.md\"\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_122_show_conversation_context_window_usage.md:14:Show the percentage of the selected conversation's context window that is used in the action popup, beside the existing total-token usage at the left of the bottom action row.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_122_show_conversation_context_window_usage.md:20:`ActionUsageSummary` displays aggregate token usage for the action and card in `ActionPopupBottomRow`. The popup already exposes `controller.displayedConversation`, but the summary does not receive it.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_126_bottom_of_action_popup_not_visible.md:5:title: Bottom of action popup not visible\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_126_bottom_of_action_popup_not_visible.md:14:On mobile, when action popup fully expanded, the bottom bar is not visible. It is hidden behind android buttons. We should leave some space\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_127_action_popup_expanded_default.md:14:On mobile, when the action popup is opened, show expanded by default. This is currently already done for card popup\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_95_after_action_name_change_actions_not_correctly_refreshed.md:14:I changed the label of an action, which changed the filename. Now the action had already been used during the run of the application. When a new action-popup was opened, the prompt could not be prepared for the action.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_95_after_action_name_change_actions_not_correctly_refreshed.md:16:on the ui, the action was using the new label, but it produced an error while trying to prepare the prompt, no prompt was built and the error still referred to the old action file.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_131_add_tooltip_to_model_setup.md:14:in the action popup and app bar, we have a set of dropdowns to set up the model and related security. add tooltips to all dropdowns so it is clear what they are for.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_147_live_update_token_usage_action_popup.md:5:title: Live update token usage action popup\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_147_live_update_token_usage_action_popup.md:14:To investigate: i think token count on action popup is only at end of conversation updated. I think we can do better\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\action_popup.md:10:- Agent actions show run-specific prompt input and agent, model, and thinking-level selection.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\action_popup.md:16:- The built-in `custom prompt` action is always available in supported contexts.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_151_improve_tool_call_box_in_chatlog.md:5:title: improve tool-call box in chatlog\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_151_improve_tool_call_box_in_chatlog.md:16:in [F\\_137\\_group\\_toolcalls.md](design/releases/0_1_0/F_137_group_toolcalls.md) we already implemented grouping of tool calls in the chatlog. only issue: all tool calls are still in their own box, the boxes are now just aligned so they touch each other.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\actions.md:15:  - `prompt`: required for an agent action.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\actions.md:27:- `prompt` and `command` can contain placeholders:\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\actions.md:30:  - `card-prompt`, containing the additional prompt entered when the card action runs.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\actions.md:44:  \"prompt\": \"use '/implement-feature' to implement {{card-file}}\",\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\actions.md:74:- Activating an entry point opens the action popup for the action `id` and selected context.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_153_action_part_in_approval_required.md:32:> \"C:\\Windows\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe\" -Command '$featurePath = '\"'C:\\Users\\janbo\\Documents\\dev\\md2\\design\\feature_descriptions\\F_151_improve_tool_call_box_in_chatlog.md' \"'$content = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText($featurePath) $updatedContent = [System.Text.RegularExpressions.Regex]::Replace($content, '\"'(?m)\"'^status: ready for implementation'\"\\r?\"'$'\"', 'status: ready', 1) if (\"'$updatedContent -eq $content) { throw '\"'Expected feature status was not found.' } \"'$utf8WithoutBom = New-Object System.Text.UTF8Encoding($false) [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText($featurePath, $updatedContent, $utf8WithoutBom)'\r\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_153_action_part_in_approval_required.md:38:> $featurePath = 'C:\\Users\\janbo\\Documents\\dev\\md2\\design\\feature_descriptions\\F_151_improve_tool_call_box_in_chatlog.md'\r\ndesign/architecture\\current_model_react.md:152:├─ prompt / command\r\ndesign/architecture\\current_data_model.md:26:| Conversations | [action_conversation_picker.tsx](C:/Users/janbo/Documents/dev/md2/app/src/components/actions/action_conversation_picker.tsx:36), `ActionPopupContent`, `useActionPopupController` | Conversation records are selected by compound activity reference; card ownership uses stable `cardInternalId`. |\r\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_156_when_approval_request_is_shown_hide_phrases.md:33:- When an approval request is visible in an action popup, that popup does not contain the predefined-phrase drawer.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_157_file_selector_popup_resizable.md:21:`ResizablePopper` already provides anchored resizing, viewport limits, accessible resize handles, and JSON `{ height, width }` persistence in `window.localStorage`. Its only production caller is the action popup, whose current behavior must remain unchanged.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_157_file_selector_popup_resizable.md:32:- Preserve current popup theme, caret anchoring, stack position above an owning action popup, listbox semantics, option rendering, and virtualized scrolling.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:5:title: remove custom-prompt as hardcoded action\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:14:On the action popup, we currently  have 2 ways to use custom prompts:\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:16:* `custom prompt` button\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:19:this is too much. 'custom-prompt' should be renamed to '+'  and the '+' should be removed.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:21:There is however a difference between the two: '+' shows an input dialog to provide a name for the new action. this input can also be removed. We will be adding a different way for adding actions from custom prompts soon, so the backend functions can remain.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:25:`md2.custom-prompt` is a shared built-in agent action. Its `Custom prompt` label makes it a normal action toggle in every supported popup. `ActionPopup` also owns a separate `Add action` (`+`) button. Clicking that button selects `md2.custom-prompt` and enables conversion mode: the popup shows a preset-name input, adds a `Save` button, and changes Send and keyboard submission from running the prompt to saving a reusable action before running it.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:27:Both routes therefore start from the same custom-prompt action, but only the separate `+` route exposes prompt-to-action conversion. The renderer's conversion flow calls the existing action-definition writer and project persistence path. The built-in action's stable ID is also used by action execution and conversation continuation, so removing that built-in would break behavior unrelated to this UI duplication.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:31:* Keep built-in action ID `md2.custom-prompt`, agent behavior, availability, and backend prompt-to-action conversion functions unchanged. Change its shared display label from `Custom prompt` to `+`; all consumers then use one canonical label.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:32:* Render that built-in as an ordinary mutually exclusive action toggle. Give its `+` control an accessible custom-prompt name and tooltip so symbol meaning does not depend on sight or prior knowledge.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:34:* Remove popup conversion-mode state and handler. `ActionPopup` only owns selected action and height state; selecting `+` follows same selection path as every other action.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:35:* Remove preset-name field and conditional save controls from popup content. Bottom row no longer shows `Save`, and Send or keyboard submission always runs current custom prompt without first creating an action file.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:36:* Remove conversion-mode conditions from popup run validation. Empty custom prompts remain blocked by existing `md2.custom-prompt` validation.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:37:* Keep action-definition writer, persistence bridge, and conversion helpers available for future custom-prompt action creation UI; this feature only removes their current popup entry point.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:38:* Update shared-definition, popup, selector, prompt-shortcut, and bottom-row tests. Cover one visible `+` action, accessible naming, direct custom-prompt execution, absent preset-name and Save controls, and unchanged empty-prompt blocking.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:42:* Each supported action popup shows one custom-prompt entry, displayed as `+`; no separate `Add action` button exists.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:43:* Assistive technology identifies `+` as custom prompt, and hover or focus explains its purpose.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:44:* Selecting `+` opens normal custom-prompt controls without showing a preset-name input or `Save` button.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:45:* Sending or keyboard-submitting non-empty text from `+` runs `md2.custom-prompt`; it does not create an action definition before or after the run.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:46:* Empty custom prompts cannot run.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:47:* Existing action definitions, run requests, conversation continuation, and histories keep stable action ID `md2.custom-prompt`.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_135_remove_custom_prompt_as_hardcoded_action.md:48:* Existing backend prompt-to-action conversion and action-definition writing functions remain available and tested, although this popup no longer calls them.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_160_unify_agent_permission_modes.md:45:- Replace the access-level and approval-policy selectors in the app bar, action popup, action editor, and config page with one permission-mode selector.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_161_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:5:title: improve bottom buttons row on action popup\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_161_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:14:we need to improve the way that the buttons are displayed on the action popup. These are the rules:\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_161_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:29:`ActionPopupBottomRow` renders Stop, Finish, Schedule, Send, and Run controls. During an active agent session (`queued`, `running`, or `waitingForInput`), Schedule remains visible but disabled. Send remains visible for an active agent and is disabled until input can be sent. During `waitingForInput`, Stop and Finish can both be visible.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_161_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:35:- In `ActionPopupBottomRow`, derive button visibility from run status and trimmed prompt text. Treat `queued` and `running` as running states; handle `waitingForInput` separately.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_161_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:43:- Extend `action_popup_bottom_row.test.tsx` and relevant popup integration coverage for each visibility state, live prompt changes, Ctrl+click, long press, confirmation outcomes, click suppression after long press, tooltips, and existing live and orphan cancellation/finish paths.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:5:title: wrong prefill of input box on action popup\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:21:basically, the rule is simple: is there something in the chatlog history? then don't prefill the input\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:25:Before this fix, selecting a stored conversation clears the prompt draft. `ActionAgentPromptOwner` then treats a completed selected conversation as eligible for prompt preparation, so the stored action prompt refills the input. The same sequence occurs when the popup automatically selects the newest unseen conversation. An unseen conversation has `viewed: false`; newest means greatest `startedAt`. An existing conversation means any selected persisted conversation, even when its `entries` array is empty.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:29:- Prepare the stored action prompt only when no agent session is active, the run is not completed, and no conversation is selected.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:30:- Keep the prompt empty after manual or automatic selection of any existing conversation, regardless of conversation status or entry count.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:31:- Preserve stored-prompt prefill for a new empty conversation. A new empty conversation means the popup has no selected persisted conversation and no active agent session.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:35:- Opening an agent action with no selected conversation and no active session prefills the input with the stored action prompt.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:36:- Selecting any existing conversation clears the input and does not prepare or apply another stored prompt.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\B_104_wrong_prefill_of_input_box_on_action_popup.md:37:- Automatically selecting the newest unseen conversation leaves the input empty and does not prepare or apply another stored prompt.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_162_more_improve_bottom_buttons_row_on_action_popup.md:5:title: more improve bottom buttons row on action popup\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_163_unify_action_usage_summary_scopes.md:18:Make `tokens`, `changes`, and `lines` in the card action popup use one explicit, user-selectable scope.\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:135:        class ActionPopup\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:136:        class ActionPopupContent\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:381:    AgentChatFab --> ActionPopup\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:410:    ActionEntryPoints --> ActionPopup\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:411:    CardRunButton --> ActionPopup\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:412:    ActionPopup --> ActionPopupContent\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:413:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionAgentForm\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:414:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionConversationChat\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:415:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionConversationPicker\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:416:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionPhraseButtons\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:417:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionRunHistory\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:418:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionRunStatus\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:419:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionScheduleForm\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:420:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionSelector\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:421:    ActionPopupContent --> ActionUsageSummary\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:422:    ActionPopupContent --> ResizablePopper\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:429:    ActionPopup --> ActionExecutionService : reads live execution\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:457:    TextView --> ActionPopup\ndesign/architecture\\class_relationships.md:532:    SearchControl --> ActionPopup\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\data management.md:52:  - prompts → also special folder\r\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\data management.md:58:    alteratively, prompts or actions are stored in json files. perhaps both can be used: actions are json definitions that reference prompt files.\r\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:5:title: Improve input and bottom row on action popup\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:13:We need to improve layout and position of input and bottom row. The goal is to provide as much viewing area as possible to the chatlog while providing optimal input size while editing a prompt.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:15:The bottom row should be inside the box of the input, sticky to the bottom, so no longer a gray bar at the bottom of the popup.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_166_improve_input_and_bottom_row_on_action_popup.md:17:When the input box has no value (empty), it should be 1 line high, box itself ofcourse more for border and bottom row. The resize bar should be disabled.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\timers.md:8:  - the user selects a date and time on the action popup\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\timers.md:11:- on the action popup, \"Schedule\" button, in front of the Run button\r\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_93_action_popup_finish_button_disabled.md:5:title: action popup finish button disabled\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_93_action_popup_finish_button_disabled.md:13:The 'finish' button on the action popup should remain disabled while the agent is still rendering output and not waiting for a response.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:5:title: no prefill prompt running conv\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:10:>>>>>>> f_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:21:When an agent is waiting for a response, but the action popup was closed or on the wrong 'action', then when the user clicks on the action to view the conversation and answer, the input box is prefilled again with the action's prompt. this is annoying cause it needs to be removed.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:27:`useActionPopupController` prepares an action's stored prompt for a new conversation. When popup opens on another action, or reopens while execution state is be