ng restored, that prepared prompt can remain in `promptState` when user selects action with a `queued`, `running`, or `waitingForInput` conversation.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:31:- Give active execution its own prompt identity, including before active-child metadata arrives.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:33:- Invalidate pending prompt preparation and bump `promptResetToken` when action becomes active.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:34:- Keep stored-prompt prefill for idle actions starting new conversations. Keep command actions unchanged.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:38:- Selecting or reopening action with active conversation does not prefill its stored action prompt.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:40:- Late prompt-preparation result cannot overwrite active conversation input.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_94_no_prefill_prompt_running_conv.md.bak:41:- Idle agent actions still prefill stored prompt.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:5:title: Improve agent selectors on action popup\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_165_improve_agent_selectors_on_action_popup.md:17:Second, we need to move it from top to bottom. On the bottom row where token-usage and buttons are. Tehe selector is to the left (fist in box), token-line-change centered, buttons to the right.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\action_editor.md:22:- The built-in `custom prompt` action is not a project file and is not shown in the tree or opened in an editor tab.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\action_editor.md:24:  - card view opens the action popup;\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\action_editor.md:35:  - the `prompt` of an agent action.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\action_editor.md:36:- Agent prompt editors provide toolbar insertion and `{{` typeahead for `{{card-file}}`, `{{card-prompt}}`, and `{{rootProjectFolder}}`.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\action_editor.md:59:| `prompt` | Required Markdown prompt for an `agent` action. |\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\action_editor.md:104:- The renderer does not execute `command` or `prompt` directly or pass executable definition data to the desktop bridge.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:5:title: card popups should behave like action popups\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:27:Card action popups differ. `CardActionPopupService` stores one stable entry per open popup, `CardActionPopupHost` renders all entries, and `ResizablePopper` supports dragging, eight-direction resizing, persisted desktop size, and activation by pointer or keyboard focus. Entry order supplies `stackPosition`; highest position means top popup.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:34:- Keep one entry per card and popup kind. Opening action popup follows current toggle behavior. Opening already-open card-details popup closes it; opening another card adds a second entry instead of replacing first.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:35:- Give card-details entries card internal ID, current path, anchor plus fallback anchor, and their own diff selection. Update matching paths after card rename. Card deletion closes only matching card-details entry. Project change clears all entries; leaving board view closes card-details entries without closing action popups.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:45:- Desktop can keep multiple card-details popups open, including while multiple card action popups remain open.\ndesign/feature_descriptions