s\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:47:- Clicking, focusing, dragging, or resizing any card or action popup brings that popup above every other managed popup. Activation does not close, remount, move, or reset another popup.\ndesign/feature_descriptions\\F_164_card_popups_should_behave_like_action_popups.md:50:- Card rename keeps matching popup open on new path. Project change clears all managed popups; leaving board view closes card-details popups while preserving action popups.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\running_actions.md:12:- The action popup and conversational panel use the same live execution state.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\running_actions.md:22:- The renderer never supplies an action command, prompt template, chain definition, or other executable definition data.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\running_actions.md:33:  - resolve placeholders in its `prompt`;\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\running_actions.md:34:  - combine the resolved prompt with run-specific prompt input;\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\running_actions.md:72:- Activating an action entry point for a card, file, folder, or supported context opens the action popup for that action and context.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\running_actions.md:74:- Agent actions also provide run-specific prompt input and agent, model, and thinking-level selection. Definition values are preselected; run-specific changes do not modify the action definition.\ndesign/architecture\\initial description\\writings\\running_actions.md:120:- Electron resolves the persisted action definition, linked action ids, placeholders, agent configuration, `prompt`, and `command`.\ndesktop\\src\\shell\\local_bridge_dispatch.test.mjs:17:        prepareActionPrompt: vi.fn(async () => ({ prompt: 'Prepared prompt' })),\ndesktop\\src\\shell\\local_bridge_dispatch.test.mjs:55:       